###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Training (Table A3): ALPB stage on 4 H200 GPUs (MoE 839,244 steps,
# compact 1,678,488 steps); DFT-SMD stage on 4 H100 (MoE) or 2 A100
# (compact) GPUs, 345,852 steps. An SNAr screen of about 4,000
# optimisations and transition-state searches took 68 GPU-hours; one
# metadynamics walker of alanine dipeptide ran at 84 ms per step on an A100
# MIG instance (system size not stated). Training wall times are not
# given.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Solvation energies are per molecule in eV and solvation forces are compared as force magnitudes. The compact model shares the UMA-S/eSEN backbone without experts and is recorded under the registry method eSEN; the MoE model is a UMA model.
# - Errors against experiment (Table III, Table A5), SAMPL6 RMSEs, zwitterion and Menshutkin errors are property errors and are not encoded. Test errors of the charge-separation augmentation are not stated separately.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
